{
  "version": 1,
  "title": "ArcCivs 0.1.52 demand-driven carpentry",
  "assumptions": [
    "Low/base/high are sensitivity assumptions: 1/5/10 owners, one supplied carpenter per owner, 0.25/1/4 active hours per day, not observed sessions.",
    "The unchanged 60000 ms production interval bounds one carpenter to 60 recipe batches per active hour; walking, hunger, night, storage, demand and receipts reduce this.",
    "The item scenario is an upper envelope with unlimited actual plank demand. Real demand-driven production stops when demand is satisfied.",
    "One real native recipe is consumed per batch. Missing external inputs, locked recipes and full output prevent completion.",
    "Current SELL is active; future SELL removal and contract transition are distinct, unchanged scenarios. No item-to-currency exchange is assumed."
